7592186501062 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "646d465e-4f31-55a7-9533-68a3a82b8349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186500870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186500489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501079 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "848eb4e6-ce36-56ea-a0f1-8a1fe68b6389" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501162 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501162 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61300" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501162 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501162 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 25%=90,$ then what is the missing number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501162 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "449615c3-fdfe-5f50-a3b0-a60b4eb31574" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501162 #edb/ref 1074 "The part is $90,$ the percentage is $25%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $25%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}=\\frac{25÷25}{100÷25}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =90÷25% \\\\  & =90÷\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =90\\times \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =90\\times 4 \\\\  & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501178 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501178 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501178 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501178 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 20%=14,$ then $\\,\\boxed{}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501178 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "706f9bb5-de0a-5c75-aa53-ea495445a284" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501178 #edb/ref 1074 "The part is $14,$ the percentage is $20%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $20%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =14÷20% \\\\  & =14÷\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =14\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =14\\times 5 \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501191 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501191 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61346" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501191 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501191 #edb/ref 1071 "On a math test, Kevin answered $95%$ of the problems correctly. If he answered $38$ problems correctly, how many problems were on the test?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501191 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87c3bda2-8545-5669-83e3-84c3d08222b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501191 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of problems answered correctly, which is $38.$ The percentage is $95%,$ and the whole is the total number of problems on the test. \n\nTo solve this question, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $95%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{95}{100}=\\frac{95÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{19}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =38÷95% \\\\  & =38÷\\frac{19}{20} \\\\  & =38\\times \\frac{20}{19} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{19}\\times 20 \\\\  & =2\\times 20 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $40$ problems on the test." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-185091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501207 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}$\\times \\,30%=24.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0060ce0-85fa-5c15-8314-02a2f37da794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501207 #edb/ref 1074 "The part is $24,$ the percentage is $30%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $30%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{100}=\\frac{30÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =24÷30% \\\\  & =24÷\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =24\\times \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3}\\times 10 \\\\  & =8\\times 10 \\\\  & =80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $80\\times 30%=24.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501210 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501210 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501210 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501210 #edb/ref 1071 "A school's softball team lost $18%$ of the games they played last year. If the team lost $9$ games last year, how many games did the team win?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501210 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2281cf7-5deb-5971-96fe-4f78cb0692fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501210 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to know the total number of games played to determine the number of games won. \n\nWe're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of games the team lost, which is $9.$ The percentage is $18%,$ and the whole is the total number of games played. \n\nTo find the whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $18%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{18}{100}=\\frac{18÷2}{100÷2}=\\frac{9}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =9÷18% \\\\  & =9÷\\frac{9}{50} \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{50}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}\\times 50 \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played by the softball team last year was $50.$ The total number of games won is\n\n$$\n50-9=41.\n$$\n\nHence, the softball team won $41$ games last year." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501211 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501211 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501211 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501211 #edb/ref 1071 "$14%$ of{{field-1}}\nis $7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501211 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b23ca4fe-ec69-5d5b-b163-9360e0e9626e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501211 #edb/ref 1074 "The part is $7,$ the percentage is $14%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $14%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{100}=\\frac{14÷2}{100÷2}=\\frac{7}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =7÷14% \\\\  & =7÷\\frac{7}{50} \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{50}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7}\\times 50 \\\\  & =1\\times 50 \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $14%$ of $50$ is $7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
